Two call replacements the scalar one could not make, each under its own name
so a report reads which answer survived. The scalar replacement's constant
truncates to false on a call returning bool, so every bool-returning call was
mutated to a predicate answering no and never to one answering yes:
cxx_replace_bool_call_true is the other answer. A call returning a pointer had
no replacement at all: cxx_replace_pointer_call_null answers it with the null
pointer of its type. The junk detector matches each against the call
expression of the return kind it names, and cxx_calls carries both names so a
configuration naming that group is unchanged. The IR half is in
tools/mull/libirm-call-replacement-header.patch.
